<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lichfield</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lichfield is a cathedral city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/staffordshire">Staffordshire</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chad">Chad</a> established the seat of the Mercian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> there in 669, and under King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/offa-of-mercia">Offa</a> it was briefly an archbishopric, from 787 to 803. Its three-spired medieval cathedral holds the 8th-century Lichfield Angel and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lichfield-gospels">Lichfield Gospels</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/staffordshire-hoard">Staffordshire Hoard</a> was found nearby in 2009.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lichfield.jpg" alt="Lichfield" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Cc44332211 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lichfield-Cathedral-June2020.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
